{"result":[{"name":"scene-create","description":"Create new scene in the project assets. Use 'scene-list-opened' tool to list all opened scenes after creation."},{"name":"scene-get-data","description":"This tool retrieves the list of root GameObjects in the specified scene. Use 'scene-list-opened' tool to get the list of all opened scenes.

Path-scoped reads (token-saving): supply 'paths' (a list of paths) to read only the listed fields/elements from the scene's root-GameObjects array via Reflector.TryReadAt, or 'viewQuery' (a ViewQuery) to navigate/filter the same array via Reflector.View. The result populates 'Data' on the returned SceneData. These two parameters are mutually exclusive.
Path syntax: 'fieldName', 'nested/field', 'arrayField/[i]', 'dictField/[key]'. Leading '#/' is stripped. Example: paths=['[0]/name'] reads the name of the first root GameObject."},{"name":"scene-list-opened","description":"Returns the list of currently opened scenes in Unity Editor. Use 'scene-get-data' tool to get detailed information about a specific scene."},{"name":"scene-open","description":"Open scene from the project asset file. Use 'assets-find' tool to find the scene asset first."},{"name":"scene-save","description":"Save Opened scene to the asset file. Use 'scene-list-opened' tool to get the list of all opened scenes."},{"name":"scene-set-active","description":"Set the specified opened scene as the active scene. Use 'scene-list-opened' tool to get the list of all opened scenes."},{"name":"scene-unload","description":"Unload scene from the Opened scenes in Unity Editor. Use 'scene-list-opened' tool to get the list of all opened scenes."}]}
